>Every so often, such as recently in this newsgroup, and just last month
>in (I think) rec.games.misc, people start asking about the saved game
>core-dumping problem.
>
>The fact is that there really is no such bug in the released 0.75. Check
>any official comp.sources.games archive, such as ftp.uu.net. This bug
>is not in there, and the sources there are over 3 years old. This is
>how the game was officially released.
>
>Apparently people still occasionally look on rutgers for the sources, but what
>can be found there is actually a version slightly before the one actually
>released.
>
>Folks, in general please use the officially archived versions of released
>software. Unless the author says something to the effect of "feel free to pick
>up my latest version at my home site", you are risking just the sort of thing
>that happened. (The author released the official version and didn't update the
>one on his home machine, probably because he didn't think that one was needed
>any more.)
>--
